  "solution": "The logic followed here is :\n\n \n• **2nd number = Square of 1st number**\n \n• **3rd number = Cube of 1st number **\n\n**​**Given :\n\n \n• (9, 81, 729)\n\n​81 = (9)²\n\n81 = 81 (LHS = RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n729 = (9)³\n\n729 = 729 (LHS = RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n \n• (14, 196, 2744)\n\n​196 = (14)²\n\n196 = 196 (LHS = RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n2744 = (14)³\n\n2744 = 2744 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo,\n\n \n• Option - (1) : (11, 212, 464)\n\n​212 = (11)²\n\n212 ≠ 121 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n464 = (11)³\n\n464 ≠ 1331 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• **Option - (2) : (17, 289, 4913)​**\n\n**​289 = (17)²**\n\n**289 = 289 (LHS = RHS)**\n\n**And,**\n\n**4913 = (17)³**\n\n**4913 = 4913 (LHS = RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (3) : (25, 625, 9375)​\n\n​625 = (25)²\n\n625 = 625 (LHS = RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n9375 = (25)³\n\n9375 = 15625 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (4) : (15, 375, 1125)​\n\n​375 = (15)²\n\n375 ≠ 225 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n1125 = (15)³\n\n1125 ≠ 3375 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nHence, **\"Option - (2)\"** is the correct answer.\n\n4c:T20f4,",
